target/
# Cargo.lock IS COMMITTED for this tree, deliberately — do not re-add it here.
#
# It was ignored until 2026-08-20 (#445), a leftover from cargo's default for a LIBRARY
# crate. cairn_pgx is not a library anyone depends on: it is a DEPLOYED ARTIFACT, a shared
# object loaded into a running PostgreSQL, and the one that enforces the in-DB safety floor.
# For a deployed artifact the lockfile is the record of what was actually built, and the
# repo's other two trees (root workspace, cairn-gui) have always committed theirs.
#
# The gap this closed was not theoretical. With no committed lock, `cargo pgrx install`
# re-resolved dependencies on every CI run, and on 2026-08-20 that resolve selected the
# compromised `arrayref` 0.3.10 and tried to fetch `proc-macro1` — a typosquat that would
# have executed AT COMPILE TIME inside the extension. It failed only because crates.io had
# already removed the typosquat; in the window before that removal, this build would have
# taken it. Two of three trees were pinned; the most safety-critical one was not.
